title The pen that planted a number the law had moved
prompt the baton, read cold -- take the next agent-doable lap in the core-infrastructure lane
think Opened with fleet_round_open (clean, on the anointed order at 61b71e4b04) and a full cold roster in the background, then held the tree still for its 846 seconds, because REDS %199's own account records a lap that edited while its pass ran and measured its repair instead of its tree.
think Council rota, lap N = 4018, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes. The fixed seat is the happy zone and the thin edge, and it named this lap's find before I had it: a control IS a happy-zone instrument, and this one had gone brackish the day the law moved.
think The cold pass read 3 red, and two were the bound meters the card names for this seat. Took both rather than the register-meter work, because a tier lap red on eight ships withholds every roster receipt, which is fleet friction rather than one tree's fault.
obs FAULT ONE, one argument. tools/fixtures/l/living_pin_max_bytes.sh answers per page; thirteen calls reach it across eight files, six bare because they print the general number and seven passing the page they weigh. reds_ledger_scan.sh:125 was the one bare call weighing a page, so a 33,200-byte ledger met 24,576 four hours after the law seated 40,960 for it.
obs FAULT TWO, a different shape in the same clothes. living_pin_near_bound_control.sh planted its page sizes as ABSOLUTES -- 24,000 was 97.6% of construction/REDS.md's bound the day the case was written and 58.6% of it overnight -- so a case labelled near planted a page nowhere near, and three of nine failed at once.
obs The pen's refusal was correct and its REPORT was not: seated_pin_named=no, over_bound_named=no, near_silent_when_hung_off_over=yes, and not one of them said the plants had gone stale. So the repair is two-part -- derive every plant from the fixture, and add case 0, plants_agree_with_law, which states the pen's own precondition and prints first. Proven to bite by spelling REDS_NEAR=24000 back in, where it answers no and names the cause in one line.
obs THE TRANSFERABLE SENTENCE: a pen that plants an absolute is testing a snapshot of the law; a pen that plants a ratio is testing the law.
obs AND THE CLASS IS INVISIBLE TO THE GUARD BUILT FOR IT. declared_ceiling_scan.sh's fourth reading gates any meter that DECIDES with a copy of the bound and exempts *_control.sh by file role, because a control PLANTS (REDS %199). Every size that broke here -- 24,000, 25,616, 24,100, 52,000 -- spells no bound at all, so a literal search finds the three sites that never moved and misses the four that did. A plant sized from the bound is a decision wearing planting's clothes.
obs Swept the whole class rather than the one red: living_docs_roster_control.sh (a page AT the bound, one past, and well past) and declared_ceiling_control.sh (a pin OVER it) now read the fixture too. Measured after: zero non-comment lines in any tracked control spell a stated bound. declared_ceiling_control.sh case 22 deliberately keeps grepping the law itself -- a pen that plants reads through the fixture, and a pen that verifies the fixture reads the law, or the check is tautological.
obs MEASURED RATHER THAN INFERRED, and it changed what I could claim. Four equinox scans consume the ledger scan; I first read three failures as my fix unblocking them, then checked which ones actually REACH the call and only equinox_e113 does. Proven both ways on metal by restoring the HEAD scan through the original inode: e113 exits 1 against HEAD and 0 against the repair -- and it had already printed a verdict=ok line from an earlier section, so its tail read like a pass over a scan that never finished.
obs CLOSED %446 as well, since it is this seat's and its own named mechanism has landed: the four legs that LAUNCH the jail moved to agent_jail_enclosure behind capability jail_nesting, and this pass reads agent_jail green 1s beside skipped_capability agent_jail_enclosure. The row's cost claim is now false in the right direction -- shell_dialect alone withholds the receipt.
obs SEATED the baton clause named for this seat, and made it more precise than the card asked: readme_metrics regenerates AFTER git add because its scan counts with git ls-files, which reads the index; geode_libraries walks with find and does not care, so after staging is right for one page and irrelevant to the other.
obs THE CARD IS AT ITS CEILING, and this lap paid it three times -- 41,326, then 41,012, then 40,997, trimming its own entry to fit. It closes at 40,776 of 40,960 only because closing %446 freed a paragraph. The next ship to write a sentence reds it. A finished section wants folding to a shelf, and that is the first job of the next lap in this lane.
obs THE LEDGER HEADLINE moved 458 -> 459 and its remainder 438 -> 439, caught by reds_ledger_monotone rather than by me. That is the card's own lantern -- a number a hand types that a peer's landing falsifies -- fired a fourth time, and here an instrument was already listening.
